    </div>
    <div class="content-split-copy reveal visible">
      <div class="chapter">TRADITION &amp; WATERFALLS</div>
      <h2>Old Lahaina &amp; Wailele Polynesian Luau</h2>
      <h3>1. Old Lahaina Luau: Embracing Tradition</h3>
      <p>The Old Lahaina Luau stands as a beacon of authenticity, drawing inspiration from the rich history and cultural tapestry of Hawaii. Nestled in Lahaina, this luau invites guests to step back in time with its traditional Hawaiian feast, complete with imu-roasted pig, poi, and other local delicacies. The evening is complemented by captivating hula performances and live music, creating an immersive experience that transports visitors to a bygone era.</p>
      
      <h3 style="margin-top: 24px;">3. Wailele Polynesian Luau: Waterfall Wonderland</h3>
      <p>Nestled in the West Maui Mountains, the Wailele Polynesian Luau at The Westin Maui Resort &amp; Spa offers a unique twist to the traditional luau setting. Surrounded by lush greenery and overlooking a cascading waterfall, this luau captivates guests with a stunning natural backdrop. The evening includes cultural performances, a delectable buffet, and the chance to witness the mesmerizing stories of the Polynesian people unfold under the starlit Hawaiian sky.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

